{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgduzZ8ewPLMnRSmYGV8b", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01J1cqY7s2WALadsWvATpjhb", "name": "Write", "input": {"file_path": "<work>\\spec.json", "content": "{\n  \"claim\": \"For an idealized, steady-state (tau >> tau_E), spatially uniform, impurity-free equimolar D-T magnetic-confinement plasma with T = T_i = T_e and n = n_i = n_e, the triple product needed for a given fuel gain is n T tau_E = 3T^2 / [ (f_c + 1/Q_fuel) <sigma v>(T) eps_F / 4 - C_B T^{1/2} ] (Eq. triple_product_steady_state). The test is the minimum over T of this required triple product, and the temperature where the minimum occurs, for Q_fuel = 1 (fuel breakeven) and Q_fuel = infinity (ignition).\",\n  \"quantities\": [\n    {\n      \"key\": \"dt_min_triple_product_qfuel_1\",\n      \"description\": \"Minimum over T (T in keV, T = T_i = T_e) of n T tau_E = 3 T^2 / [ (f_c + 1/Q_fuel) <sigma v>_DT(T) eps_F / 4 - C_B T^{1/2} ] with Q_fuel = 1. Take the minimum only where the denominator is positive. Here n is the total ion density (n = n_i = n_e, equimolar D-T, Z = 1, uniform profiles, no impurities). Inputs: eps_F = 17.6 MeV (3.5 MeV alpha + 14.1 MeV neutron), f_c = 3.5/17.6 (alpha fraction), 1 MeV = 1.6e-13 J, C_B = 5.34e-37 W m^3 keV^-1/2. <sigma v>_DT is the thermal Maxwellian D-T reactivity from Bosch & Hale (1992); the paper numerically integrates the Bosch-Hale cross section, and the Bosch-Hale reactivity parametrization is an acceptable equivalent. Report the full-precision minimum value.\",\n      \"units\": \"m^-3 keV s\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"dt_temperature_at_min_triple_product_qfuel_1\",\n      \"description\": \"The temperature T (= T_i = T_e) at which the Q_fuel = 1 triple product n T tau_E in dt_min_triple_product_qfuel_1 reaches its minimum, with the same equation, assumptions and inputs. Report at full precision.\",\n      \"units\": \"keV\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"dt_min_triple_product_qfuel_inf\",\n      \"description\": \"Minimum over T (T in keV, T = T_i = T_e) of n T tau_E = 3 T^2 / [ f_c <sigma v>_DT(T) eps_F / 4 - C_B T^{1/2} ], i.e. the same expression with Q_fuel -> infinity (ignition, 1/Q_fuel = 0). Take the minimum only where the denominator is positive. Assumptions and inputs are the same as for dt_min_triple_product_qfuel_1: total ion density n = n_i = n_e, equimolar D-T, uniform profiles, eps_F = 17.6 MeV, f_c = 3.5/17.6, 1 MeV = 1.6e-13 J, C_B = 5.34e-37 W m^3 keV^-1/2, Bosch-Hale D-T reactivity. Report the full-precision minimum value.\",\n      \"units\": \"m^-3 keV s\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"dt_temperature_at_min_triple_product_qfuel_inf\",\n      \"description\": \"The temperature T (= T_i = T_e) at which the Q_fuel = infinity (ignition) triple product n T tau_E in dt_min_triple_product_qfuel_inf reaches its minimum, with the same equation, assumptions and inputs. Report at full precision.\",\n      \"units\": \"keV\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"paper_values\": {\n    \"dt_min_triple_product_qfuel_1\": 4.6e20,\n    \"dt_temperature_at_min_triple_product_qfuel_1\": 14,\n    \"dt_min_triple_product_qfuel_inf\": 2.9e21,\n    \"dt_temperature_at_min_triple_product_qfuel_inf\": 14\n  },\n  \"redact\": [\n    \"$\\\\mathrm{D+T}$ &              1 &                        14 &                                 \\\\num{4.6e+20}\",\n    \"$\\\\mathrm{D+T}$ &       $\\\\infty$ &                        14 &                                 \\\\num{2.9e+21}\"\n  ],\n  \"not_computable\": \"\"\n}\n"}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "timestamp": "2026-11-02T10:06:24.376Z", "request_id": "req_011CgduzYtXc2KiDmuswLe4M", "wire_tool_inputs": {"toolu_01J1cqY7s2WALadsWvATpjhb": {"file_path": "<work>\\spec.json", "content": "{\n  \"claim\":