{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cgdv1oUteHewygDbee3Zk", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I wrote `spec.json`. It covers the two D-T rows of Table 3 (minimum triple product needed in magnetic confinement): the minimum value of n\u00b7T\u00b7\u03c4_E and the temperature where it occurs, at Q_fuel = 1 and Q_fuel = \u221e, for uniform profiles.\n\n**What's in the spec**\n- **Four quantities**: the minimum triple product and its temperature at each of the two gain values. Each is defined by the paper's triple-product equation (lines 686\u2013689) with these inputs:\n  - 17.6 MeV released per reaction (3.5 MeV alpha plus 14.1 MeV neutron), with the charged fraction f_c = 3.5/17.6\n  - 1 MeV = 1.6e-13 J\n  - bremsstrahlung constant C_B = 5.34e-37 W m\u00b3 keV^-1/2\n  - the Bosch & Hale (1992) D-T reactivity, which the next agent can use from memory as a cited standard formula\n- **Paper values**:\n\n| Q_fuel | Minimum n\u00b7T\u00b7\u03c4_E (m\u207b\u00b3 keV s) | Temperature at minimum (keV) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 4.6e20 | 14 |\n| \u221e | 2.9e21 | 14 |\n\n- **Redactions**: just the two D-T table rows (lines 709\u2013710). I checked that both strings are unique and match the file's spacing exactly.\n- **`not_computable`**: left empty, because the calculation is a one-dimensional minimisation that can be rebuilt from the paper.\n\n**Things I checked or chose**\n- **No other leaks**: I searched the abstract, the text around the table, the figure captions, and the sections on uneven profiles and other fuels. None of them repeat these numbers. The line saying the triple-product minimum sits at a lower temperature than the Lawson-parameter minimum is qualitative, so I left it in.\n- **Table 2 left visible**: its D-T minimum Lawson parameters (26 keV) are a different result and don't reveal the Table 3 values.\n- **Reactivity method**: the paper integrates the Bosch-Hale cross sections numerically rather than using their ready-made reactivity fit. The spec accepts the fit as an equivalent, so small differences in the last digits could come from that choice."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "timestamp": "2026-11-02T10:06:33.576Z", "request_id": "req_011Cgdv1oCmntvpHV5D4L4Nq"}
